# LaTeX build artifacts and scratch renders (regenerate with: python build.py)
build/
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz

# No assembled volume and no PDF is ever published. Only the Markdown chapters
# and the projects are, which is what mdbuild.py writes. These are blanket rules
# rather than named files, so a new output name cannot slip through: the whole
# volume, a single unit of it, or anything else.
*.pdf
*.html

# Named explicitly as well, so the intent survives anyone relaxing the rules
# above.
embedded-linux-kit-labs.pdf
embedded-linux-kit-labs.html

# Per-lab deliverables, built on demand with: python build.py --chapter N
lab-*.pdf
lab-*.html

# Local virtual environments and editor state
.venv/
venv/
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The labs' own evidence. A capture is what one bench produced on one day, a
# lab book is the baseline and thresholds that belong to it, and a run report
# is the numbers of one recording, so none of them is source. Regenerate a
# synthetic one with: ./p04 synth, or ./p18 synth
*.p04
*.lab
*.p18
*.stream
*.capture
*.book
*.glass
*.transcript
*.p13
test_p06_sysfs/

# What building the labs leaves behind: objects, dependency files and the
# binaries. Rebuild with: make -C p04, make -C p18
*.o
*.d
p02/p02
p02/p02-test
p03/p03
p03/p03-test
p04/p04
p04/p04-test
p06/p06
p06/p06-test
p13/p13
p13/p13-test
p18/p18
p18/p18-test
lib_atchat.o

# What a local run of the checks workflow leaves behind
touch.txt
speech.txt
p02/timers.txt
p02/plan.txt
p02/attached.txt
p02/searching.txt
p03/fix.txt
p03/nofix.txt
p06/base.txt
p06/mixed.txt
p18/clean.txt
p18/long.txt
p02-suite.txt
p03-suite.txt
p04-suite.txt
p06-suite.txt
p13-suite.txt
# p13 names its scene reports after the scene, in a loop, so these are a glob
p13/*.txt
p18-suite.txt

# Journals and correspondence never reach a published repository, private
# shares included. They live in the catalogue, which is local only. A published
# repository carries the work, never the running record of doing it. This is a
# guard rather than a reminder: the rule has held by discipline so far, and a
# rule that lives only in someone's head is one copy away from being broken.
private_journal/
correspondence/
DIARY*.md

# The authoring sources are not published. Only the Markdown edition is, with
# its SVG figures beside it. A reader takes one chapter, not a book, and a
# chapter is a .md file. The .tex that generates it stays on the authoring
# machine, which is why lint.py, checkcode.py and mdbuild.py have nothing to
# read in a fresh clone and why prepublish.py exists to run them locally.
#
# This is a blanket rule rather than named folders, so a new source file
# cannot slip through: sections/, figures/*.tex, main.tex and the preamble are
# all covered by the one line.
*.tex
